<body>
<div class="wrap">
<header>
  <h1>How this board works</h1>
  <p class="tagline">CandidateZero is a jobs board that checks its own listings.
  This page explains what that means, in plain words.</p>
</header>
<main class="prose">
<section>
  <h2>What "verified live" means</h2>
  <p>Every listing on the board was re-fetched from the employer's own hiring system
  during the most recent run. Not copied from an aggregator, not scraped from another
  jobs board, not remembered from last month. The engine goes to the same place your
  application would go and confirms the posting is still there.</p>
  <p>When a role stops appearing on the employer's system, it comes off the board the
  same night and spends a week in the "closed recently" section, so you can see what
  quietly disappeared.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>Which systems are checked</h2>
  <p>The engine reads company hiring pages served by six systems: Ashby, Greenhouse,
  Lever, Workable, SmartRecruiters, and Workday. If a company runs its hiring on one
  of these, its board can be watched and its listings can be verified.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>How titles are matched</h2>
  <p>Roles are matched by title family, not by keyword. The board asks whether the
  title itself names a GTM engineering, RevOps or revenue systems job, the way a
  person reading it would. A keyword search would drag in every posting that mentions
  "revenue" somewhere in the text; a family match keeps the board to roles where the
  title is the job.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>What the board does not show</h2>
  <p>No personal filters, no application history, no compensation floors. Those belong
  to individual job seekers and stay private. Everyone who reads this board sees the
  same listing, built by one public rule: the title fits the family and the posting is
  live on the employer's own system. Compensation appears only when the employer
  publishes it, and is never estimated or invented.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>The engine never applies for anyone</h2>
  <p>Every apply link goes straight to the employer's own posting. The board does not
  collect resumes, does not forward applications, and does not sit between you and the
  company in any way. It reads, verifies, and lists. That is all.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>How fresh is this data</h2>
  <p>Last completed run: {{ report.last_run }}. Each run re-reads every watched
  company board, so nothing listed as live is older than the most recent run.</p>
</section>
</main>
